        "id": 153365,
        "name": "dpt",
        "username": "dpt",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/dpt/{size}/1922_2.png",
        "created_at": "2016-01-18T20:56:00.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"Rabit\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/rabit/48/5774_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Rabit:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Often an RPG is set in a world populated by characters that tell a story around the actions of the player characters (PCs). The story of the PCs might dip in and out of the story of other characters, but those other stories are happening around them, regardless. It really depends on the game / campaign setting, though.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>I also wouldn't be surprised if there are one-shot scenarios to play through that tell the story of some adventure of the main heroes, like the War of Heliopolis. I think it's already clear that you will be able to play as Legacy/Wraith etc (as in the demos at GenCon etc), as well as create your own characters.</p>\n<p>EDIT: For that matter, what was the scenario at GenCon? Is it part of the canonical storyline?</p>",
        "post_number": 21,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T04:32:41.703Z",
