      {
        "id": 153366,
        "name": "Silverleaf",
        "username": "Silverleaf",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/silverleaf/{size}/2332_2.png",
        "created_at": "2016-01-18T22:47:47.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p><span>I was thinking of the RPG as a physical place to put background and stories and character information, because it's an important part of the setting.</span></p><p><span>It seems very natural to use all that stuff as \"fluff\" even if you don't choose to use pre-existing characters.</span></p><p><span>White Wolf products have a lot of that kind of thing, with lots of descriptions about different factions/people/areas/etc, and some short stories/vignettes to help you get a feel for the flavour of stories you're likely to create in your own games.</span></p><p><span>What I'd like to see for SC:RPG is general world-flavour in the main section of the book, and descriptions of the environments. I'd put character sheets and bios of existing characters as an appendix at the back. [i]Proper[/i] bios, with up-to-date history, so we can use it both as a resource for the RPG and as general reference material for us Sentinerds.</span></p>",
        "post_number": 22,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T04:32:41.761Z",
